{
  "about": "Dragging selected text, as on a Mac (docs/adr/0037-text-editing.mdx, decision 9; docs/adr/0035-drag-and-drop.mdx): sample/TextDragProbe.tsx's Bloom fields (a single-line one, a multiline one, and one with maxLength 12 inside a drop target taking text) and sample/TextDragPeer.tsx, another application started beside it (`companion`), with a row of text it drags and two drop targets taking text, one copying unless asked otherwise and one that only moves. A press on the selection released without moving places the caret where it was pressed; moved, it drags the selected text. Within the field the drop moves it (Option copies), one edit that one undo takes back, the text moved left selected. Into another field it copies, that field taking focus with the text selected, focus, change and selectionChange its only events; a field inside a drop target takes the text dropped on it, the drop target hearing only the pointer pass over its own edge. Out to the other application's copying target it arrives once and the field keeps it; to the moving one the field deletes it. Text dragged in from the other application drops into a field; a field keeps only what maxLength leaves room for; Escape cancels with nothing changed. With Command a drag into another field moves: the field it left, no longer focused, deletes the text as an edit of its own, and an undo in the other takes back only its insertion. Each step's React events and deliveries to both applications are exact. At scale 1.25 (a 1600x1000 display, 1280x800 logical).",
  "module": "TextDragProbe",
  "window": [
    640,
    420
  ],
  "companion": {
    "module": "TextDragPeer",
    "window": [
      280,
      240
    ],
    "at": [
      980,
      200
    ]
  },
  "outputs": "1600x1000@1.25",
  "steps": [
